  "prediction": "**Amy Schumer Makes Two Big Announcements: Pregnancy and Midterm Elections**\n\nComedian Amy Schumer has made two significant announcements recently. Firstly, she revealed that she is expecting her first child with husband Chris Fischer. The news was shared on Instagram by Jessica Yellin, a former CNN Chief White House Correspondent, who also promoted Schumer's support for the #NewsNotNoise campaign.\n\nSchumer's pregnancy announcement was cleverly tied to a voting reminder, as she directed her followers to Yellin's Instagram page to learn about the upcoming midterm elections. Yellin shared Schumer's picks for candidates in the elections, and at the bottom of the list, revealed Schumer's pregnancy news.\n\nThis is not the first time Schumer has used her platform to promote social and political causes. She has been a vocal advocate for gun control, the transgender community, and has supported Colin Kaepernick's peaceful protest of the NFL. Earlier this month, she was reportedly detained and arrested for protesting Brett Kavanaugh's nomination to the Supreme Court.\n\nSchumer has also been critical of the NFL, urging Maroon 5 to pull out of the Super Bowl Halftime Show in support of Colin Kaepernick's protest. In a recent Instagram post, she challenged white NFL players to kneel in solidarity with Kaepernick, writing, \"Otherwise how are you not complicit?\"\n\nIn related news, Schumer has decided not to appear in any Super Bowl LIII commercials this year, citing her support for Kaepernick's protest and her desire to \"hurt\" the NFL by opposing it. This decision is in line with her previous stance on the NFL, which she has criticized for its handling of player protests.\n\nOverall, Amy Schumer's pregnancy announcement has been a clever way to promote voting and social awareness, and is a testament to her commitment to using her platform for good.",
